"""Verified rank-3-signotope flip-path generator for arXiv:2310.19711.

The paper identifies marked pseudoline arrangements with rank-3 signotopes and
triangle flips with single sign changes.  This module builds a shortest
monotone flip interval from the all-minus signotope to a signotope whose plus
triples share two curves.  Four-set packet monotonicity forces the changed
triples into one order.  That order is labelled, in four consecutive blocks,
by cubic permutation polynomials over a displayed prime field.

The answer is the four polynomials, not a long path.  The checker expands the
polynomials and replays every triangle flip using the signotope axiom.  The
generator samples the polynomials first and never solves the instance it made.
It is deterministic in ``(n, seed, params)``, standard-library-only, and has no
import-time side effects.
"""

