   157	```
   158	
   159	`verify(inst, answer)` returns `(True, "ok")`. Removing the last vertex returns
   160	`(False, "wrong part sizes: expected [4, 3, 3, 3], got [4, 3, 3, 2]")`.
   161	
   162	## Difficulty
   163	
   164	| preset | n | retained edges | reference operations | status |
   165	|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
   166	| demo | 13 | 65 | 101 | hand-solvable illustration |
   167	| easy | 37 | 296 | 476 | local gates pass; oracle call blocked |
   168	| medium | 109 | 872 | 1,736 | local gates pass; not reached by oracle |
   169	| hard | 229 | 1,832 | 3,884 | configured shipping preset; oracle evidence pending |
   170	
   171	The next admissible size has more than 256 answer atoms, so `escalate` correctly
   172	returns `"cap_bound"` after hard rather than pretending the family has no
   173	further scale.
   174	
   175	## Gate results
   176	
   177	| gate | result |
   178	|---|---|
   179	| G1 | pass, 12/12 planted certificates |
   180	| G2 | pass, five corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
   181	| G3 | pass, tagged JSON round-trip with prose/fence |
   182	| G4 | pass, 0/200,000 structure-aware guesses; 443-bit candidate space |
   183	| G5 | pass locally; shipping density 0/200,000, demo has exactly 6/92,400 answers, reference cost 3,884 operations |
   184	| G6 | pass; degree, consecutive, residue-mod-4, quadratic-character, 256-restart, and 256-node DPLL attacks each succeed 0/8; reference succeeds 8/8 |
   185	| G7 | pass; n=541 builds and verifies |
   186	| G8 | pass; 80/80 invariance, 80/80 carried witnesses, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
   187	| G9(c) | pass; 1,043 characters, 261 estimated tokens, 229 atoms, 228 intended operations |
   188	| G9(a,b) | **pending** because every official oracle request returned HTTP 403 |
   189	
   190	## Oracle loop and G9 arms
   191	
   192	No solved/failed model attempt exists yet: the harness redraws provider errors
   193	and then aborts, as it should. The counts below therefore remain 0/0 rather
   194	than misreporting API failure as hardness.
   195	
   196	| run | preset | valid solved/attempts | recorded outcome |
   197	|---|---|---:|---|
   198	| bare | easy | 0/0 | four HTTP 403 quota errors; harness aborted |
   199	| structural hint | hard | 0/0 | four HTTP 403 quota errors; harness aborted |
   200	| placebo hint | hard | 0/0 | four HTTP 403 quota errors; harness aborted |
   201	
   202	Hinted minus placebo is unavailable. No conclusion about the claimed intuition
   203	can be drawn until these arms run successfully.
   204	
   205	## Use
   206	
   207	```python
   208	import gen_2310_15909 as g
   209	
   210	inst = g.make_instance(seed=7, **g.DIFFICULTY["demo"])
   211	statement = g.render(inst)
   212	ok, reason = g.verify(inst, inst["answer"])
   213	assert (ok, reason) == (True, "ok")
   214	```
   215	
   216	From the repository root, after successful oracle reruns and updating
   217	`G9_EVIDENCE`:
   218	
   219	```bash
   220	scripts/emit.sh 2310.15909 20 hard
   221	```
   222	
   223	## Caveats
   224	
   225	The quartic structure is generator-specific, not a theorem of the paper; the
   226	paper supplies the parity obstruction that makes the certificate sound. A
   227	tool-enabled solver finds the partition quickly, which is why this is Track B.
   228	The 0/200,000 estimate is relative to uniformly random exact-size ordered
   229	partitions with both anchors already placed in `V0`; it is not a probability
   230	under every solver prior and does not establish complexity-theoretic hardness.
   231	The attack panel includes a standard-library DPLL baseline with unit and
   232	cardinality propagation, but not an industrial SAT/SMT or CP solver; it also
   233	reports the faster distribution-specific character algorithm. Sparse edge
   234	thinning may admit certificates unrelated to the planted cosets. At medium and
   235	hard there are fewer retained edges than an STS would require, so nonexistence
   236	itself is also visible by edge count; the graded object is specifically the
   237	paper's executable four-part parity certificate. Finally, no
   238	LLM-hardness claim is currently justified: rerun the three official harness
   239	arms once OpenRouter quota is restored, inspect replies for parser bugs, update
   240	`G9_EVIDENCE`, rerun `selftest()`, and only then treat `hard` as shipped.

